course: dictionary
lesson: 10191
title: One word, many meanings: timetable
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A timetable is a list or chart that shows what happens at what time. Your school timetable tells you which lesson comes at which time each day. A bus or train timetable does the same job for transport.
explain: Context helps you choose the right meaning. «Learn your school timetable and check it the night before, so you bring the right things and know where to be.» Here it means the list of lessons. In «Buses keep to a timetable and don't wait», it means the times buses leave and arrive.
explain: Timetable can also be a verb: to timetable something means to plan it for a certain time. In «Grief has no timetable», the word is a noun, and it means grief does not follow a set plan for when it stops. Always check which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: Do not mix timetable up with times tables. «Times tables» are multiplication facts like 7 × 8 = 56. A timetable is a plan of times. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A timetable is a list or chart showing what happens at what time.
fact: Timetable can also be a verb: to timetable something is to plan it for a certain time.
fact: In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, your school day is shown on a timetable; in the USA people often say «schedule».
fact: French timetables use the 24-hour clock, so «14h30» means half past two in the afternoon.
fact: «Times tables» are different: they are multiplication facts, not lists of times.
exercise: «Learn your school timetable and check it the night before.» What does timetable mean here? | A bus that runs late | A table of numbers you learn to multiply | A wooden table in the classroom | *A list of lessons and the times they happen
exercise: «Buses keep to a timetable and don't wait.» What does timetable mean here? | A map of roads and bus stops | A stick used to measure time | *A list of the times buses leave and arrive
exercise: Your teacher says, «Let's timetable the art project for Friday.» What does timetable mean here? | Ask the class to vote on it | *Plan it for a certain time | Paint it in lots of colours | Throw the project away
test: On a train timetable, what does 14h30 show? | Fourteen minutes past three | Half past one in the afternoon | Midnight | *Half past two in the afternoon
test: Which one is a times table rather than a timetable? | *7 × 8 = 56 | A list of bus leaving times | A chart of lessons for Tuesday
exam: Ruby says, «Grief has no timetable.» What does she mean? | Grief is a multiplication fact | Grief has a list of set days when it stops | *Grief does not follow a set plan, so it can come back at any time | Grief is a kind of school lesson
